This is a **singleplayer** bridge. LAN host is fine. A dedicated server is not.

Pick the jar that matches your Minecraft version. 1.21.1 through 1.21.11 wants Java 21. The 26.x jars want Java 25. The wrong jar will just sit in the folder.

Open a singleplayer world with cheats on. Leave it loaded. The local API only exists while that integrated server is running. Pause menu is fine. Title screen is not.

Then point TikFinity at this machine. That is the next page.

If you are testing without a live audience, you can still fire commands from any ServerTap-style client. Same port, same idea.
